usage: opencl_executor.py [-h] [--width WIDTH] [--batch BATCH]
                          [--layers LAYERS] [--policy-mib POLICY_MIB]
                          [--device-ids DEVICE_IDS [DEVICE_IDS ...]]
                          [--reverse] [--inject-corruption] [--output OUTPUT]

Experimental, policy-bounded mixed-vendor residual MLP executor. This proves
one host-staged OpenCL workload. It is not an LLM runtime, allocator, durable
worker system, physical-capacity measurement, or P2P test.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --width WIDTH
  --batch BATCH
  --layers LAYERS
  --policy-mib POLICY_MIB
  --device-ids DEVICE_IDS [DEVICE_IDS ...]
                        OpenCL runtime IDs pN:dN; default selects one NVIDIA
                        and one AMD GPU
  --reverse             Reverse selected device order
  --inject-corruption   Corrupt the real activation at the first device
                        boundary
  --output OUTPUT       Atomically write bounded JSON result
